cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these codes, please cite the article given as the preferred citation."
title: "tduality-bh: codes for the global and dynamical viability of the T-duality-inspired Bardeen regular black hole"
abstract: >-
  Python, Julia and Maple codes accompanying the article "Global and dynamical viability of
  the T-duality-inspired Bardeen regular black hole" by D. Batic and D. Dutykh, Annals of
  Physics 496, 170842 (2027). The Python scripts draw the figures of the article (geodesic
  potentials, radial diagnostics of the core, light rings, horizons and surface gravities,
  the filtered mass inflation, proper times) and check the closed form of a Bessel moment;
  the Maple worksheets and the Julia solver compute quasinormal modes of scalar and
  electromagnetic test fields by Chebyshev collocation in high precision.
